1
00:01:19,079 --> 00:01:20,622
Found it.

2
00:01:24,918 --> 00:01:27,045
Nice! Nice, nice.

3
00:01:28,463 --> 00:01:30,172
Great. Thanks for your hard work.

4
00:01:30,173 --> 00:01:31,465
I'll be there soon.

5
00:01:31,466 --> 00:01:33,300
<i>- Hang tight.</i>
- Okay.

6
00:01:33,301 --> 00:01:35,929
He killed them here,
then moved them to a freezer.

7
00:01:40,600 --> 00:01:42,477
But there's no sign of the tiger.

8
00:01:43,019 --> 00:01:45,813
<i>That's okay. You said there's a cage.</i>

9
00:01:45,814 --> 00:01:47,940
<i>I'll put out another APB now.</i>

10
00:01:47,941 --> 00:01:50,527
It looks like
he's been working on something.

11
00:01:51,486 --> 00:01:54,155
Huh? A stage?

12
00:01:56,241 --> 00:01:58,076
What's this?

13
00:02:10,046 --> 00:02:11,131
There's a note.

14
00:02:13,466 --> 00:02:14,592
It's in Hangeul.

15
00:02:15,677 --> 00:02:18,388
- I'll send you a picture.
<i>- Okay, I'll check it out now.</i>

16
00:02:33,945 --> 00:02:35,029
<i>Hello?</i>

17
00:02:35,530 --> 00:02:36,489
<i>Hello?</i>

18
00:02:37,532 --> 00:02:40,285
I'm sorry. I'll call you back.

19
00:02:44,414 --> 00:02:45,456
What's up with him?

20
00:02:50,503 --> 00:02:52,005
<i>Kim Seok.</i>

21
00:02:54,215 --> 00:02:56,134
Detective Kim Seok.

22
00:02:59,762 --> 00:03:01,096
SEOUL POLICE
KIM SEOK'S MOTHER

23
00:03:01,097 --> 00:03:02,347
Kim Seok?

24
00:03:02,348 --> 00:03:04,017
MARIA NURSING HOME

25
00:03:58,696 --> 00:04:01,115
THE BLUE ROAD

26
00:04:04,535 --> 00:04:06,120
Please help me.

27
00:04:06,704 --> 00:04:08,122
Please help me.

28
00:04:08,957 --> 00:04:09,874
Please.

29
00:04:17,757 --> 00:04:18,882
What happened exactly?

30
00:04:18,883 --> 00:04:21,802
A young man came to visit your mother
and took her with him.

31
00:04:21,803 --> 00:04:23,596
He was Japanese.

32
00:04:25,223 --> 00:04:26,849
We've been looking for her, but...

33
00:04:29,394 --> 00:04:31,145
Ms. Lee Ae-gyeong!

34
00:04:31,688 --> 00:04:33,939
- Are you okay?
- Where are you?

35
00:04:33,940 --> 00:04:36,149
Ms. Lee, where are you?

36
00:04:36,150 --> 00:04:37,192
Where are you?

37
00:04:37,193 --> 00:04:38,694
Ms. Lee Ae-gyeong!

38
00:04:38,695 --> 00:04:40,570
Can you hear my voice?

39
00:04:40,571 --> 00:04:42,490
Where are you?

40
00:04:43,199 --> 00:04:44,659
Ms. Lee Ae-gyeong!

41
00:04:45,618 --> 00:04:47,953
- Where are you?
- Can you hear my voice?

42
00:04:47,954 --> 00:04:50,872
Ms. Lee Ae-gyeong!

43
00:04:50,873 --> 00:04:52,165
Where are you?

44
00:04:52,166 --> 00:04:54,085
Ms. Lee Ae-gyeong!

45
00:05:18,901 --> 00:05:19,902
Mom!

46
00:05:23,323 --> 00:05:24,532
Mom!

47
00:05:26,951 --> 00:05:29,996
Mom! Mom!

48
00:05:30,496 --> 00:05:31,456
Mom!

49
00:05:36,085 --> 00:05:36,919
Mom.

50
00:05:42,842 --> 00:05:44,510
Don't move. Stay right there.

51
00:05:47,013 --> 00:05:47,972
It's dangerous.

52
00:05:49,682 --> 00:05:50,892
Mother.

53
00:05:52,852 --> 00:05:53,728
Who am I?

54
00:06:08,368 --> 00:06:09,618
Are you hurt?

55
00:06:09,619 --> 00:06:11,079
Who are you?

56
00:06:13,998 --> 00:06:15,416
Mom, it's me. Seok.

57
00:06:18,044 --> 00:06:19,711
Mom. Mom.

58
00:06:19,712 --> 00:06:21,546
- Get away from me, bastard!
- Mother!

59
00:06:21,547 --> 00:06:22,923
Get away!

60
00:06:22,924 --> 00:06:24,674
- Mom! It's me, Seok!
- Let go of me!

61
00:06:24,675 --> 00:06:26,719
- Get away from me, you bastard!
- Mom!

62
00:06:27,387 --> 00:06:30,181
- You worthless bastard. Get away!
- Mother!

63
00:06:30,681 --> 00:06:32,350
- You're okay.
- Go away, you bastard!

64
00:06:32,934 --> 00:06:33,934
Mother!

65
00:06:33,935 --> 00:06:35,894
Are you okay?

66
00:06:35,895 --> 00:06:37,313
Is she okay?

67
00:06:38,022 --> 00:06:39,148
Inose...

68
00:06:43,361 --> 00:06:44,987
And who are you?

69
00:06:46,239 --> 00:06:48,574
Who the hell are you?

70
00:06:49,367 --> 00:06:50,493
Hello.

71
00:06:52,453 --> 00:06:54,414
My name is Inose Hiroshi.

72
00:06:55,456 --> 00:06:57,542
I'm a friend of Detective Kim's.

73
00:06:58,418 --> 00:07:00,795
How dare you, you Japanese bastard!

74
00:07:01,295 --> 00:07:04,339
My husband!

75
00:07:04,340 --> 00:07:05,549
You killed him.

76
00:07:05,550 --> 00:07:08,802
You Japanese bastards killed my husband!

77
00:07:08,803 --> 00:07:11,138
Get out. Can't you hear me?

78
00:07:11,139 --> 00:07:13,849
Get out of here, you Japanese bastards!

79
00:07:13,850 --> 00:07:17,060
Seok, your uncle.

80
00:07:17,061 --> 00:07:18,812
Where's Uncle Du-yeong?

81
00:07:18,813 --> 00:07:20,981
Seok. Where's Uncle Du-yeong?

82
00:07:20,982 --> 00:07:22,984
- It's okay.
- Seok.

83
00:07:24,944 --> 00:07:26,194
Du-yeong.

84
00:07:26,195 --> 00:07:29,406
Du-yeong! Du-yeong!

85
00:07:29,407 --> 00:07:32,326
Du-yeong!

86
00:07:33,369 --> 00:07:34,203
Du-yeong...

87
00:07:52,013 --> 00:07:53,639
<i>She has Alzheimer's.</i>

88
00:07:55,683 --> 00:07:57,018
She's had it for a while.

89
00:08:04,859 --> 00:08:06,568
She wasn't in her right mind,

90
00:08:06,569 --> 00:08:09,030
so please don't take
what she said to heart.

91
00:08:11,491 --> 00:08:12,867
I'm truly sorry.

92
00:08:15,745 --> 00:08:17,955
It's fine. No biggie.

93
00:08:18,539 --> 00:08:20,833
I couldn't understand anything anyway.

94
00:08:25,171 --> 00:08:26,506
My mother...

95
00:08:28,758 --> 00:08:30,718
was a <i>mudang</i> who served the gods.

96
00:08:32,303 --> 00:08:35,056
A Korean shaman.

97
00:08:43,689 --> 00:08:45,358
People were afraid of her.

98
00:08:49,612 --> 00:08:51,072
And so was I.

99
00:08:59,121 --> 00:09:00,289
And your father?

100
00:09:01,374 --> 00:09:03,626
His work was similar to my mother's.

101
00:09:05,211 --> 00:09:06,921
He was a geomancer.

102
00:09:08,422 --> 00:09:10,298
He traveled the country

103
00:09:10,299 --> 00:09:13,511
digging up iron stakes the Japanese buried
during their occupation.

104
00:09:14,720 --> 00:09:18,349
Digging out those iron stakes
that had been buried for decades.

105
00:09:19,850 --> 00:09:22,270
So, an anti-Japanese campaign of sorts.

106
00:09:23,187 --> 00:09:24,272
But then,

107
00:09:25,022 --> 00:09:26,941
he went missing.

108
00:09:29,527 --> 00:09:31,696
We don't even know if he's dead or alive.

109
00:09:32,530 --> 00:09:35,825
After that,
I grew up under my uncle's care.

110
00:09:37,368 --> 00:09:39,203
The man my mom was calling for earlier.

111
00:09:40,580 --> 00:09:43,958
Saying, "Du-yeong, Du-yeong!"

112
00:09:47,962 --> 00:09:51,215
<i>He'd sought out my mother
to learn the trade.</i>

113
00:09:53,551 --> 00:09:56,220
<i>Before long, he filled the void
my father had left behind.</i>

114
00:10:05,146 --> 00:10:06,856
Where is this uncle now?

115
00:10:09,650 --> 00:10:10,776
Ah...

116
00:10:12,111 --> 00:10:13,487
He died.

117
00:10:16,824 --> 00:10:20,745
That's when my mother's condition
started to worsen.

118
00:10:24,040 --> 00:10:26,459
I fear I may have overshared.

119
00:10:28,252 --> 00:10:29,337
I'm sorry.

120
00:10:35,092 --> 00:10:36,552
Thank you...

121
00:10:38,220 --> 00:10:39,055
for telling me.

122
00:10:43,434 --> 00:10:45,102
But what matters to us...

123
00:10:47,730 --> 00:10:50,775
is catching this pesky culprit.

124
00:10:59,367 --> 00:11:02,203
The hallway of
the nursing home had a security camera.

125
00:11:02,703 --> 00:11:03,537
As you can see,

126
00:11:04,205 --> 00:11:06,290
it's like the bastard wanted to be filmed.

127
00:11:06,791 --> 00:11:08,668
He wanted us to see.

128
00:11:09,627 --> 00:11:12,213
But how did he know your mother was there?

129
00:11:12,713 --> 00:11:16,132
He's a clever bastard
who used his detention to his advantage.

130
00:11:16,133 --> 00:11:19,637
It can't have been hard to get
the hospital address from a neighbor.

131
00:11:21,931 --> 00:11:23,265
He's toying with us.

132
00:11:24,475 --> 00:11:26,018
While flaunting himself.

133
00:11:30,564 --> 00:11:32,733
The sly motherfucker.

134
00:11:33,234 --> 00:11:34,985
Hold on. Hold on!

135
00:11:36,570 --> 00:11:37,779
Zoom in on this.

136
00:11:37,780 --> 00:11:39,490
- Zoom in?
- Yes.

137
00:11:43,661 --> 00:11:45,287
What is this bastard saying?

138
00:11:45,788 --> 00:11:46,914
Re...

139
00:11:47,623 --> 00:11:48,456
Rehear...

140
00:11:48,457 --> 00:11:50,167
Rehearsal?

141
00:11:51,460 --> 00:11:52,503
Rehearsal?

142
00:11:53,170 --> 00:11:54,922
Ah, in other words,

143
00:11:55,673 --> 00:11:58,341
him going to see your mother
was just a rehearsal?

144
00:11:58,342 --> 00:12:00,093
So he's preparing for something?

145
00:12:00,094 --> 00:12:02,011
What are you three cooking up?

146
00:12:02,012 --> 00:12:04,639
You lunatic. Well? What is it now?

147
00:12:04,640 --> 00:12:06,642
- We're checking the footage--
- Don't.

148
00:12:07,143 --> 00:12:08,310
Not a word.

149
00:12:08,811 --> 00:12:11,647
No good ever fucking comes
from getting mixed up with you lot.

150
00:12:12,148 --> 00:12:15,316
I'm starving. What are we eating?

151
00:12:15,317 --> 00:12:16,402
Huh?

152
00:12:19,029 --> 00:12:21,991
Huh? What is this?

153
00:12:24,201 --> 00:12:25,244
What's wrong?

154
00:12:26,495 --> 00:12:27,955
There's no way.

155
00:12:28,497 --> 00:12:29,581
URGENT NOTICE

156
00:12:29,582 --> 00:12:32,167
LEE HYEON-SEO,
PATIENT UNDER POLICE SUPERVISION, MISSING

157
00:12:32,168 --> 00:12:37,256
Okay, everyone.
Let's all practice how we'll cheer!

158
00:12:37,757 --> 00:12:41,050
Do you all know the cheer
that's on TV everywhere these days?

159
00:12:41,051 --> 00:12:44,220
The one where you clap five times.
You know the drill, right?

160
00:12:44,221 --> 00:12:45,473
Let's give it a go.

161
00:12:47,224 --> 00:12:48,934
Republic of Korea!

162
00:12:50,478 --> 00:12:51,895
Republic of Korea!

163
00:12:51,896 --> 00:12:54,397
Hold on. Today's our first game, everyone.

164
00:12:54,398 --> 00:12:57,108
We need to give it everything we've got.
What do we say?

165
00:12:57,109 --> 00:12:58,985
Republic of Korea!

166
00:12:58,986 --> 00:13:00,653
Whoo!

167
00:13:00,654 --> 00:13:02,448
Republic of Korea!

168
00:13:04,492 --> 00:13:06,285
Republic of Korea!

169
00:13:13,083 --> 00:13:14,752
What about the officers there?

170
00:13:17,546 --> 00:13:21,508
Uh, all personnel were deployed
to City Hall and Gwanghwamun

171
00:13:21,509 --> 00:13:23,427
due to the World Cup cheering events.

172
00:13:24,053 --> 00:13:25,930
This is why he called it a rehearsal.

173
00:13:26,764 --> 00:13:28,224
Hyeon-seo is the main event.

174
00:13:30,100 --> 00:13:34,103
To the hospital. Now!
We move fast but quietly. Got it?

175
00:13:34,104 --> 00:13:36,523
- We don't have time. Move!
- Lead team, go.

176
00:13:36,524 --> 00:13:37,525
Yes, sir!

177
00:13:40,444 --> 00:13:42,362
Let's make this a public investigation.

178
00:13:42,363 --> 00:13:43,738
- We need to hurry.
- Move.

179
00:13:43,739 --> 00:13:45,908
- For fuck's sake!
- You little shit!

180
00:13:46,826 --> 00:13:48,201
Forgot your place?

181
00:13:48,202 --> 00:13:50,954
The vehicle, the composite sketch,
or the sighting on CCTV.

182
00:13:50,955 --> 00:13:53,039
We don't have time
to get this to the press.

183
00:13:53,040 --> 00:13:56,085
So you want to advertise
that a crazy killer is on the loose?

184
00:13:57,670 --> 00:13:59,797
It's so we can catch him.

185
00:14:01,173 --> 00:14:02,925
The boss said no.

186
00:14:03,676 --> 00:14:05,344
Because of the World Cup.

187
00:14:11,559 --> 00:14:12,810
Start the car.

188
00:14:17,189 --> 00:14:21,068
Calm down. Deep breaths, deep breaths.

189
00:14:26,240 --> 00:14:27,323
First, the hospital--

190
00:14:27,324 --> 00:14:29,409
No. Then it'll be too late.

191
00:14:29,410 --> 00:14:32,246
- So what do you suggest?
- We need to think.

192
00:14:40,921 --> 00:14:42,839
Emi is an artist.

193
00:14:42,840 --> 00:14:45,175
A perfectionist
who constantly craves approval.

194
00:14:45,718 --> 00:14:49,513
That's why he hasn't slipped up once.

195
00:14:53,058 --> 00:14:54,143
Could it be?

196
00:14:56,520 --> 00:14:58,605
You could come to my upcoming show.

197
00:14:58,606 --> 00:15:01,900
This time,
it'll be an interactive sound art piece...

198
00:15:01,901 --> 00:15:05,154
During his interrogation,
he said I should come see his show.

199
00:15:05,738 --> 00:15:07,323
He said it would be interactive.

200
00:15:09,950 --> 00:15:10,826
Rehearsal.

201
00:15:14,288 --> 00:15:17,123
With a bit of a performance element too.

202
00:15:17,124 --> 00:15:18,459
<i>A performance.</i>

203
00:15:20,961 --> 00:15:22,170
That's it.

204
00:15:22,171 --> 00:15:24,589
I was wondering what he meant back then.

205
00:15:24,590 --> 00:15:27,092
One second. Could you take a look at this?

206
00:15:28,260 --> 00:15:31,764
It says Emi Shunsuke is giving
a piano performance in Gunsan today.

207
00:15:35,017 --> 00:15:36,101
Gunsan.

208
00:15:36,810 --> 00:15:37,645
Yeah.

209
00:15:38,145 --> 00:15:40,480
Request backup
from the South Gunsan Police now.

210
00:15:40,481 --> 00:15:41,690
Yes, sir.

211
00:15:48,614 --> 00:15:49,739
Republic of Korea!

212
00:15:49,740 --> 00:15:51,825
SPECIAL PRE-MATCH PERFORMANCE
BY PIANIST EMI SHUNSUKE

213
00:16:00,125 --> 00:16:03,419
THE PERFORMANCE WILL BEGIN SHORTLY
PLEASE TAKE YOUR SEATS

214
00:16:03,420 --> 00:16:05,797
<i>The South Gunsan Police
aren't very keen to help.</i>

215
00:16:05,798 --> 00:16:07,256
<i>With what happened last time--</i>

216
00:16:07,257 --> 00:16:10,010
I didn't leave you there for nothing!
Keep calling them.

217
00:16:11,762 --> 00:16:12,680
Hey.

218
00:17:11,113 --> 00:17:13,032
You woke up earlier than I expected.

219
00:17:14,324 --> 00:17:17,953
I even used more anesthetic this time.

220
00:17:28,422 --> 00:17:29,757
You

221
00:17:31,050 --> 00:17:33,343
will become the greatest instrument.

222
00:17:36,430 --> 00:17:39,516
An instrument that will
live on in everyone's memories forever.

223
00:17:45,606 --> 00:17:47,858
Republic of Korea!

224
00:17:48,817 --> 00:17:50,568
<i>Hello, viewers.</i>

225
00:17:50,569 --> 00:17:52,988
<i>At last, the day
we've all been waiting for.</i>

226
00:17:53,655 --> 00:17:58,159
<i>Mr. Commentator, the atmosphere
in and around the stadium is wild.</i>

227
00:17:58,160 --> 00:18:03,540
<i>The fans are cheering so loudly
that my own voice is being drowned out.</i>

228
00:18:07,002 --> 00:18:08,711
What the...

229
00:18:08,712 --> 00:18:10,422
Oh my gosh!

230
00:18:54,633 --> 00:18:57,052
Republic of Korea!

231
00:19:05,269 --> 00:19:07,271
Republic of Korea!

232
00:19:21,410 --> 00:19:28,082
<i>Oh, victory Korea</i>

233
00:19:28,083 --> 00:19:31,545
<i>Oh, olé, olé...</i>

234
00:19:43,015 --> 00:19:44,683
We save Hyeon-seo first.

235
00:19:50,439 --> 00:19:52,065
A lift.

236
00:19:54,735 --> 00:19:56,987
<i>It was a stage lift.</i>

237
00:19:59,615 --> 00:20:00,699
<i>The tiger was there.</i>

238
00:20:02,242 --> 00:20:03,368
A lift?

239
00:20:15,547 --> 00:20:17,049
The mechanical room. Here.

240
00:20:22,429 --> 00:20:24,514
Inose. Inose! Another door! Another door!

241
00:20:52,918 --> 00:20:53,835
Let's go.

242
00:21:00,717 --> 00:21:02,134
It's okay.

243
00:21:02,135 --> 00:21:04,012
- Wait.
- You're okay.

244
00:21:05,639 --> 00:21:07,391
Look. We're the police.

245
00:21:08,308 --> 00:21:10,310
Are you okay?

246
00:21:14,690 --> 00:21:15,774
Emi Shunsuke did this?

247
00:21:18,527 --> 00:21:19,444
Emi?

248
00:21:22,447 --> 00:21:26,618
That bastard came backstage,
then he suddenly dragged me away.

249
00:21:28,620 --> 00:21:31,456
<i>And then he brought this girl</i>

250
00:21:31,957 --> 00:21:33,083
<i>and a tiger...</i>

251
00:22:00,277 --> 00:22:01,361
Thank you.

252
00:22:01,945 --> 00:22:04,948
I will now present my encore

253
00:22:05,449 --> 00:22:09,619
and the final exhibition of my life.

254
00:22:13,040 --> 00:22:14,207
Its title is...

255
00:22:15,208 --> 00:22:17,169
He said he'd let us hear it live.

256
00:22:18,670 --> 00:22:19,755
"Live."

257
00:22:20,255 --> 00:22:22,632
It's a message.

258
00:22:23,300 --> 00:22:25,760
He intends to plant fear
into the audience.

259
00:22:25,761 --> 00:22:29,723
"One fear breeds infinite fear
and all methods shall be concealed."

260
00:22:38,857 --> 00:22:41,526
<i>He intends to showcase
the moment of Hyeon-seo's death.</i>

261
00:22:44,279 --> 00:22:47,199
Is there a lift room here,
used for stage effects?

262
00:22:51,953 --> 00:22:53,080
There it is.

263
00:22:55,457 --> 00:22:56,541
The tiger.

264
00:23:56,393 --> 00:23:57,853
Ms. Hyeon-seo!

265
00:24:54,701 --> 00:24:57,078
Please... Please...

266
00:24:58,830 --> 00:24:59,789
Please.

267
00:25:00,957 --> 00:25:01,833
Wake up.

268
00:25:02,334 --> 00:25:03,501
Please wake up.

269
00:25:03,502 --> 00:25:04,461
Hey, Inose.

270
00:25:09,549 --> 00:25:10,383
Hey.

271
00:25:12,594 --> 00:25:13,595
What's going on?

272
00:25:21,770 --> 00:25:23,563
Oh...

273
00:25:29,236 --> 00:25:31,821
The detective from back then.

274
00:25:41,623 --> 00:25:44,251
Now she won't make any sound.

275
00:26:35,176 --> 00:26:36,636
Emi Shunsuke!

276
00:27:38,865 --> 00:27:40,283
That's enough. Come out now.

277
00:27:42,035 --> 00:27:43,036
Now!

278
00:27:45,413 --> 00:27:47,832
Are you sure you even want to catch me?

279
00:27:49,793 --> 00:27:52,087
Then why do you look so conflicted?

280
00:27:53,546 --> 00:27:55,757
You should be focusing on me.

281
00:29:32,270 --> 00:29:33,938
Ah...

282
00:29:34,647 --> 00:29:36,232
That's got to hurt.

283
00:29:42,155 --> 00:29:43,031
Huh?

284
00:30:03,593 --> 00:30:05,470
You having fun?

285
00:30:07,806 --> 00:30:08,973
Because...

286
00:30:13,728 --> 00:30:14,854
I still got to...

287
00:30:16,606 --> 00:30:18,733
show my performance to the two people...

288
00:30:21,069 --> 00:30:22,654
I most wanted to show it to.

289
00:30:24,239 --> 00:30:27,033
You've been infected with fear.

290
00:30:34,833 --> 00:30:37,210
Stop! Hey, Inose!

291
00:30:42,298 --> 00:30:44,592
Feel that same pain yourself.

292
00:30:49,722 --> 00:30:51,849
Hey, Inose. Inose. Inose.

293
00:30:51,850 --> 00:30:54,309
Stop!

294
00:30:54,310 --> 00:30:57,063
- Let go of me!
- That's enough. Stop it now.

295
00:31:03,236 --> 00:31:04,653
Are you okay?

296
00:31:04,654 --> 00:31:05,572
Inose.

297
00:31:08,032 --> 00:31:09,534
That's enough now.

298
00:31:10,076 --> 00:31:11,035
Okay?

299
00:31:11,536 --> 00:31:12,745
Let's arrest him now.

300
00:31:34,100 --> 00:31:35,143
No! Hey!

301
00:31:41,357 --> 00:31:43,067
If I die,

302
00:31:43,902 --> 00:31:45,028
would that be more fun?

303
00:31:48,281 --> 00:31:49,324
I'm sure

304
00:31:50,283 --> 00:31:52,994
you still have so many questions.

305
00:31:55,663 --> 00:31:56,998
The original...

306
00:32:08,092 --> 00:32:09,385
...lives.

307
00:32:28,154 --> 00:32:29,571
Snap out of it!

308
00:32:29,572 --> 00:32:31,031
Inose, hurry!

309
00:32:31,032 --> 00:32:33,493
The body from back then...

310
00:32:35,203 --> 00:32:36,537
Hong Du-yeong?

311
00:34:08,838 --> 00:34:10,547
URGENT NOTICE

312
00:34:10,548 --> 00:34:13,134
EMI SHUNSUKE PRONOUNCED DEAD
DURING TRANSPORT

313
00:34:57,386 --> 00:34:58,721
Seok.

314
00:35:02,225 --> 00:35:03,851
Seok!

315
00:35:10,316 --> 00:35:11,859
Kim Seok!

316
00:36:03,953 --> 00:36:05,663
INOSE HIROSHI

317
00:36:07,123 --> 00:36:08,499
KIM...

318
00:36:13,254 --> 00:36:18,426
THE LATE LEE HYEON-SEO

319
00:36:33,316 --> 00:36:36,569
She was too young
to have a resident registration card.

320
00:36:38,946 --> 00:36:40,573
So she doesn't have a photo.

321
00:36:58,299 --> 00:36:59,508
We failed

322
00:37:00,468 --> 00:37:01,844
to keep our promise.

323
00:37:28,496 --> 00:37:29,872
I guess this is it.

324
00:37:34,377 --> 00:37:36,295
Is it really over now?

325
00:37:54,855 --> 00:37:56,148
It was good working with you.

326
00:38:03,823 --> 00:38:05,866
Why did you let go of Emi's hand?

327
00:38:09,537 --> 00:38:10,871
My hand slipped.

328
00:38:16,002 --> 00:38:17,545
I believe I told you before...

329
00:38:20,423 --> 00:38:22,383
I really don't like people
who keep secrets.

330
00:38:32,518 --> 00:38:33,644
Hong Du-yeong!

331
00:38:43,029 --> 00:38:44,905
The uncle I told you about before.

332
00:38:46,073 --> 00:38:47,074
Hong Du-yeong.

333
00:38:53,289 --> 00:38:54,498
He was a victim.

334
00:39:02,798 --> 00:39:04,925
<i>The serial murder case in the '80s.</i>

335
00:39:09,638 --> 00:39:11,140
<i>The original...</i>

336
00:39:13,434 --> 00:39:14,643
<i>lives.</i>

337
00:39:31,911 --> 00:39:33,371
In 2002,

338
00:39:34,747 --> 00:39:38,125
there was Emi Shunsuke, a serial murderer
who contorted his victims' limbs...

339
00:39:40,002 --> 00:39:41,628
And the original from 1987,

340
00:39:41,629 --> 00:39:45,424
the serial murderer
who twisted Hong Du-yeong's limbs...

341
00:39:48,719 --> 00:39:50,262
<i>...is yet to be caught.</i>
